# C, THE COUPLING MATRIX: an OBSERVED dependence between two layers' remainders. One row per
# (filing, from_layer, to_layer), which is the sparse form of an L x L matrix.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ C = 0 IS THIS MODEL'S ASSUMPTION, SO EVERY ROW HERE IS SOMEBODY CONTRADICTING IT
#    WITH AN OBSERVATION. That is why the observation is required rather than optional: a
#    coupling is never derived, never inferred from correlation, and never filed as a
#    number alone. Somebody watched two layers move together and wrote down what they saw.
#
# ⛔⛔ AND THE ABSENCE OF ROWS SAYS NOTHING BY ITSELF. A filing with no couplings has either
#    a stack of independent layers or nobody who looked, and those are opposite claims.
#    Which one it is lives in `coupling_search` -- see epistemics/searches.sqlc -- and NOT
#    in this relation. Densify this into a grid of 0.0 and the difference is gone for good.
-- pm:Stack/pm:Couplings/pm:Coupling, each carrying its pm:observation.
SELECT c.filing, c.from_layer, c.to_layer,
       c.low, c.mode, c.high, c.unit, c.observation
FROM pm.coupling c
